silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_25_six_step_bridge_deep_dives_sections_01_mereology_six_step_concrete_anchor_6#partidentification_relator silm:hasLongDescription "The PartIdentification_relator is the relator pair (f_left_paw, f_right_paw): left paw and right paw identified as the same paw type though distinct individuals. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'PartIdentification_relator', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
